# RuyaOS presets (T-195). Fedora's own presets enable these; a console does not need them.
# 96-services.sh applies `systemctl preset` to every unit named here while the image builds, and
# masks the ones listed in MASKED there. The reason for each is in docs/image-packages.md.

# User accounts over D-Bus for desktop greeters (Flatpak pulls the package in); profiles are plain
# Unix users from useradd (ruya-profiles), not systemd-homed users.
disable accounts-daemon.service
disable systemd-homed.service
disable systemd-homed-activate.service
# Software RAID monitor and its monthly check (mdadm stays for udisks2's libblockdev).
disable mdmonitor.service
disable raid-check.timer
# No sssd/authselect profile switching; FIPS mode is not a RuyaOS feature.
disable authselect-apply-changes.service
disable fips-crypto-policy-overlay.service
# Fedora's usage counter (a network call to Fedora once a week).
disable rpm-ostree-countme.timer
# bootc's own unattended `bootc upgrade --apply`, which reboots: ruya-update owns the update
# policy (check, download, announce, restart at night when idle).
disable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
